# Preferred setup: run `strong-mcp login` once to sign in with your email +
# password. It mints and saves tokens to token.json — no secrets needed here.
#
# The token vars below are an OPTIONAL bootstrap for seeding a captured token
# pair instead of logging in. All three must be set together to be used.
# STRONG_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# STRONG_REFRESH_TOKEN=
# STRONG_DEVICE_ID=

# Optional: data dir for token.json + snapshot.json (default: ~/.strong-mcp)
# STRONG_DATA_DIR=
# Optional: dev proxy (e.g. Proxyman) http://localhost:9090
# STRONG_PROXY_URL=
# Optional: override display unit (POUNDS | KILOGRAMS); default = account preference
# STRONG_WEIGHT_UNIT=
# Optional: read-only mode over a Strong CSV export (Settings > Export Strong
# Data). No login or network needed; write tools are disabled.
# STRONG_CSV_PATH=/path/to/strong.csv
# Optional: bearer token (16+ chars) for `strong-mcp --http`. Required when
# binding to anything other than 127.0.0.1 / localhost.
# STRONG_MCP_HTTP_TOKEN=
# Optional: app version to identify as, if Strong rejects the built-in one
# (default 6.4.2 / 8332). Copy current values from a proxy capture.
# STRONG_CLIENT_VERSION=
# STRONG_CLIENT_BUILD=
